WEBVTT

00:00.750 --> 00:05.130
This is Gobo,
an open-source AI film studio built on ComfyUI.

00:05.590 --> 00:08.270
You say the film, Gobo shoots it.

00:09.730 --> 00:15.530
We first built Gobo as an in-house AI cinema
system for SuperStock and VistaLab.ai.

00:15.950 --> 00:18.550
It was designed for real commercial work.

00:19.130 --> 00:24.370
For Comfy's challenge, we took it standalone,
put it on Comfy Router, and opened the code.

00:25.730 --> 00:28.990
Type one line, pick a look,
a length, and a shape.

00:29.490 --> 00:36.100
Gobo's planner writes the shot list,
paints a keyframe for every shot, and LTX 2.5, our core video model,

00:36.150 --> 00:37.530
brings each one to life.

00:38.380 --> 00:41.580
A script supervisor checks
every cut for continuity.

00:41.840 --> 00:45.000
Then the film is cut, graded,
and ready to share with a link.

00:49.630 --> 00:50.670
Want control?

00:51.210 --> 00:54.940
Direct it yourself, camera, lens,
light, film stock, and the move.

00:54.990 --> 00:57.610
Compiled into the prompt,
a cinematographer would write.

00:58.380 --> 01:02.380
The Lab steals the look of any frame
and grades your takes like film.

01:02.960 --> 01:07.040
Using Rust,
compiled to WebAssembly right in your browser.

01:14.370 --> 01:15.780
Ready for the graph?

01:15.830 --> 01:23.450
Open in ComfyUI hands you the same shot as Gobo's own nodes,
and the same Rust code grades it there pixel for pixel.

01:28.550 --> 01:34.730
Under the hood, Python and FastAPI, plain JavaScript,
four Rust crates running in the browser and on the server,

01:34.970 --> 01:36.510
and ffmpeg for the cut.

01:37.360 --> 01:44.760
One Comfy key reaches every model, LTX, FLUX 3,
Seedance, and Nano Banana, with Claude planning the shots.

01:48.420 --> 01:51.940
Most AI video tools give you
a prompt box or a node graph.

01:52.590 --> 01:54.960
Gobo gives you a crew and a door into ComfyUI.

01:55.010 --> 01:57.170
It's It's open source.

01:57.410 --> 01:58.410
Go make a film.
